From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: defer PPE until PHY is ready

PPE connects each port to its PHY during platform probe. If the MDIO bus
is still probing, phylink returns -ENODEV for a valid phy-handle that has
not been registered yet. PPE treats that as permanent and tears the port
down for the rest of the boot.

Check a declared phy-handle before allocating the phylink path. If its
PHY device has not been registered and bound yet, defer PPE probe so the
driver core can retry once MDIO and phylib have finished bringing up the
supplier.

This is particularly important when an MDIO controller itself has a
late clock provider, but the ordering issue is generic to probe-time PHY
connections.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_net.h>
+#include <linux/of_mdio.h>
 #include <linux/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.h>
 #include <linux/phylink.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
@@ -1103,6 +1104,28 @@
 	PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10G_QXGMII,
 };
 
+static int ppe_port_wait_for_phy(struct ppe_port *ppe_port)
+{
+	struct device_node *phy_node;
+	struct phy_device *phydev;
+	int ret = 0;
+
+	phy_node = of_parse_phandle(ppe_port->np, "phy-handle", 0);
+	if (!phy_node)
+		return 0;
+
+	phydev = of_phy_find_device(phy_node);
+	of_node_put(phy_node);
+	if (!phydev)
+		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+
+	if (!device_is_bound(&phydev->mdio.dev))
+		ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
+
+	put_device(&phydev->mdio.dev);
+	return ret;
+}
+
 /**
  * ppe_port_phylink_setup() - Set phylink instance for the given PPE port
  * @ppe_port: PPE port
@@ -1119,6 +1142,10 @@
 	struct device_node *pcs_node;
 	int i, ret;
 
+	ret = ppe_port_wait_for_phy(ppe_port);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	/* Get PCS instance */
 	pcs_node = of_parse_phandle(ppe_port->np, "pcs-handle", 0);
 	if (!pcs_node)
